apple ceo tim cook this morning at the  deal book conference dropping absolute  bombs he was asked by andrew ross sorkin  hey tim do you own any bitcoin ethereum  other cryptocurrencies and here is  exactly what tim had to say do you own  crypto in any bitcoin or ethereum would  you play around with this i i do yeah i  think it's reasonable to own it as a as  a part of a diversified portfolio and  i'm not giving anybody uh investment  advice by the way  when when did you get interested in it  i've been interested in it for a while  and uh i've you know been researching it  and and and so forth and so uh i think  it's interesting so when you start to  see the leader of one of the largest  technology companies in the world saying  wait a second i do own this stuff right  and he was a little unclear we don't  know if he owns just bitcoin just  ethereum bitcoin and ethereum other  things but he owns cryptocurrencies in  general and we also don't know exactly  when he bought it we don't know how big  of a portion it is in his portfolio but  he made it seem like duh of course i do  and nobody should be surprised by this  we are talking about a technologist  somebody who literally his job is to  figure out what the most uh latest  technology trends are to figure out what  consumer behaviors are to understand  everything from hardware to software to  payments and everything in between that  is his job so of course he has taken  time to learn about this of course he's  intellectually curious about it and of  course if you understand how to learn it  is by participating he owns some of it  now it would not surprise me to see that  tim cook would be first to kind of be  orange-pilled or to start to use some of  these technologies you first put it on  your own balance sheet you start to use  some of the different products and  services in the industry and then  eventually you start around the office  saying well you know what i was using  this thing it's pretty interesting i  wonder what it would look like if we  were to incorporate some of these  technologies into our products or our  services and so is there a day in the  future where we see apple go ahead and  allow for bitcoin or other  cryptocurrency payments absolutely in my  opinion are there is there a day where  they start to integrate with things like  web 3 or some of the other products and  technologies that people are building  absolutely because ultimately if you go  back to what we've been saying now for a  while crypto is not going to be a  separate industry  instead what you are going to get is you  are going to get crypto to infiltrate  all of the existing assets in all of the  existing industries you are going to  have all of them upgrade their rails all  of them will upgrade their technologies  very similar to a bookstore that used to  just be in the analog physical world it  eventually went online well eventually  that bookstore continued to upgrade its  technologies we didn't think about an  internet bookstore after 10 or 15 years  of the internet of course every  bookstore has an online store the same  thing is going to happen in crypto  however you want to define that whether  you define it by one asset or many  assets these technologies are going to  be pervasive across society and so to  see the leader of one of the most  important most successful technology  companies saying that he owns the  technologies that he owns the assets  shouldn't be a surprise to anyone but i  think the part that we are now watching  is that people are comfortable talking  about it so there's likely that they've  actually owned the technologies for a  while is that they've owned them for  some time they've been intellectually  interested in as you just said but you  couldn't talk about it you might have  come off as crazy or insane or you lost  your mind but now all of a sudden it's  cool to talk about it of course you can  talk about it the career risk has been  removed and so whether it's tim cook  here or somebody else in a position of  power or influence whether they're in  the finance industry the technology  industry or somewhere else they now are  allowed to talk about this technology in  a way that it is  it is expected it is not a surprise to  anyone that they own it and i think that  is to me the biggest takeaway is that  now tim cook is comfortable saying that  he owns this technology and also when he  goes and he does a interview like this  he's asked about it if you go back five  years no one would have asked him about  it and also he would have been  comfortable talking about it but now we  have the questions being asked and we  have him saying it and i think that  you're only going to see this become  more and more part of the mainstream  narrative which means that more and more  people will become educated they'll  become familiarized and we will continue  to see user adoption across the industry  of all sorts of different technologies  and products and services and so tim  cook's in the game apple eventually will  get in the game as well along with every  other major technology company john were  you surprised when you saw that tim cook  owned cryptocurrencies and was so  comfortable talking about it publicly  not really right he's been in the  technology space for pretty much his  entire life um it surprised me that this  hasn't come out before he was pretty  open about it when asked about it so i'm  surprised that no one's ever actually  directly asked him in a public forum  about it um and him actually given an  answer but  i'm curious to see what apple does with  it in the future so he did mention that  apple doesn't hold any bitcoin or  anything like that because people don't  want to invest in apple and have like  that exposure to bitcoin that's not why  they're coming to invest in apple so  we'll see where it goes but does apple  accept this do they invest in companies  that are around this do they start using  the technology within their products or  services um that's where i am kind of  keeping my eye on yeah and i think  that's an important point because at the  end of the day apple's a two and a half  trillion dollar market cap company it's  one of the biggest technology companies  in the world and he's the ceo of it so i  don't think it's surprising to anyone uh  that he's experimenting or owns at least  some of kind of one of the most  disruptive technologies we've seen in  our lifetime so that's not surprising at  all i think the part that is interesting  and people should care much more about  is what apple does right as a company so  uh the follow-up question i believe with  that was like hey are you guys going to  accept payments are you going to hold  bitcoin on your balance sheet and to  john's point he said hey look we don't  want to hold it on our balance sheet not  because i don't believe in it i invested  in it  personally so there's obvious obviously  some kind of personal belief in in the  asset but we don't want to hold it  because our customers aren't buying  apple stock uh to have exposure to  bitcoin and i thought one of the  interesting things that michael saylor  said yesterday was a lot of people when  they think about what michael sailor has  done with microstrategy uh there's a  common complaint saying hey look i don't  want i didn't want to become a levered  bitcoin etf right when i bought  microstrategy stock but what most people  don't know and he talked about yesterday  was that they offered to buy back shares  at a premium if you held microstrategy  stock right so he's before they bought  it before they bought it yeah so he said  this is what we're planning to do if you  don't do not want exposure to bitcoin if  you don't want to be part of this if you  don't believe in that future direction  we'll buy your shares back from you at a  premium to its current price which is  like the most baller move of all time  right because it's like hey look we have  shareholders we care about you we want  you know it's changing it's a large set  of people but even retail small guys  that have one share of our stock we care  about you right and we want you to know  uh that this is the direction we're  going in so it's much different when it  comes to apple right it's a it's a large  large large company but the same mindset  applies where he's saying hey look we  don't think that people want to own this  necessarily when they own our stock so  maybe there's some kind of conversion  over time but it makes sense in my  opinion that's why he hasn't done it yet  will that change in the future i think  that's the big question yeah it is very  interesting also that this is all  happening and he's starting to talk  about this more as you see other major  tech companies like facebook etc start  going into these technologies and start  talking about how they're going to  leverage them uh on top of that you get  all the anti-trust pressures and the  judge ruling that uh apple does have to  allow other types of payment services  within their apps in their app store so  there's a lot of kind of complexity in  this analysis in terms of like why would  they be going into this but ultimately i  think what you do is you can you can say  okay where are we now fast forward 10 20  years and this stuff is going to be  pervasive and so of course the  incumbents they have two options either  they're going to embrace the innovative  technology and the superior technology  or they're going to get disrupted and  what literally might happen is those  that embrace it win and continue to uh  to evolve and succeed and those who  choose to ignore it end up actually  failing and so this is a story as well  as time in terms of the innovator's  dilemma are you willing to actually go  and look at the new technology are you  willing to incorporate that new  technology we just saw actually stripe  uh put matt huang from uh paradigm on  their board of directors right a payment  company saying wait a minute hold on  there's a whole new sector that we may  not be experts at but we need to go find  somebody who is an expert somebody who  does spend all day thinking about this  who's very thoughtful and say can you  come join our board of directors and can  you make sure that we do not get  disrupted by this new space and i think  that you know imagine if apple all of a  sudden not only said hey look our ceo  owns this stuff oh maybe we'll go ahead  and integrate some of the technologies  but let's go find a leader in the  industry and let's put them on our board  of directors let's hire them as an uh  advisor let's start to build some sort  of like skunk works type r d um you know  corner of the apple business that is  solely focused on these technologies  like those are all things that an  innovative company would pursue uh we  don't see that yet obviously it sounds  like they're kind of early in their  journey here but to know that the ceo  the most important person at the company  in terms of uh driving strategy and  direction of the business he's into this  stuff i think lends itself that there's  a high likelihood that they could go do  that stuff in the future yeah and i  think i think the thing to think about  too is like it only really takes a few  individuals right that own and operate  these major companies so when you think  about jack dorsey like the impact he has  had on bitcoin has been tremendous not  only from like a kind of put a stake in  the ground and say hey i believe in this  technology as kind of someone who built  multiple companies uh really well but  from his ability to go in and transform  the market right what he's done with  twitter what he's doing with square cash  app etc tim cook has that same ability  if not bigger there's i was just looking  up the numbers 113 million people use  iphones in the united states 50 50 of  smartphone users so when you think about  his ability to really make change  fundament fundamental change uh and  drive this technology forward he has uh  he has a large large large ability to do  that

